  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "This is building off of this feedback post (https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1471-vrc-constraints-cause-jitter-with-contacts-and-physbones) and was made so the problem can be highlighted a bit better.\n\nAs it stands VRC Constraints offer significant performance benefits and has added two new features: \"Solve in Local Space\" and \"Freeze in World\". The issue stems with Freeze to World having to be stuck on VRC Constraints, which makes it hard to reduce the jittering issues with regards to Physbones and Contacts. If possible I feel the solution would be simple: Have \"Freeze to World\" to be a separate component that can be scheduled before Physbones and Contacts.",
